- <strong>Ukraine and Moldova</strong> have both been granted EU candidate status.&nbsp;
<div>- Ukraine applied days after the Russian invasion in February, and the process moved at a record speed.</div>
<div>- While Moldova's application was accepted, a third former Soviet state, Georgia, has still to qualify for candidacy.&nbsp;
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Source: BBC</div>
